{"title":"2022 SSMO Relay Round 5 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_5_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1970593e80703dfe31ef799575bae2ee9819ced1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\times 8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> chessboard with a knight in one of the center squares. The knight may move in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />-shaped fashion, going two squares in one direction and one square in a perpendicular direction, but cannot go outside the chessboard. How many squares can the knight reach in exactly two moves?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_5_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 5 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_5_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. Consider sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96a65c8de69e33c20ea766d91d4639ae7b70c5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\{a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_{2022}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a624c32947a0eb99057acb1e6da6ede421754561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1\\le a_2\\le \\cdots \\le a_{2022}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6ed4874dc50b706cc9494f665554a8a1e1c4a152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{lcm}(a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_{2022})=70T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" />. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/3470df210c179bd9923b1845214832220d146633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a_i,a_j)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43efff2768fb4d7be15c052fe3d89d0dd57d9c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i&lt;j\\le2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" />. Find the number of possible sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_5_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 5 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_5_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a28f69b8173b91f4328c13d2690e8cbb2fe451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{cis}(x) = \\cos(x) + i\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7fca3ded703bf29cf5409401c60be895fb9957d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=\\operatorname{cis}\\left(\\frac{k\\pi}{T+1}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"142\" height=\"45\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2d2202535839f82ec1cccbce08c6c61d15ae5de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{T+1}\\frac{|a_{2k}+a_{2k+2}-a_{2k-1+T}|}{|a_{2k+1}-(a_{2k}+a_{2k+2})|}\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"51\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32d22fdf85b5a557c083f0b20142b57c5973013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{c})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_5_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 5 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018064512\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 76/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3059/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- 